{
  "abstain": false,
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "UPI Circle is a feature introduced by NPCI that allows UPI users to delegate payments to trusted secondary users for performing transactions within security protocols and limits.",
      "sources": ["S9"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Under the UPI Circle framework, a primary user can authorize a trusted secondary user to initiate and complete UPI transactions as per defined spend limits under Full Delegation or authorize initiation of payment requests under Partial Delegation.",
      "sources": ["S1", "S6", "S9"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Primary users are the individuals who act as the main account holders and authorize secondary users for payments.",
      "sources": ["S1", "S2", "S3", "S6", "S9"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Secondary users include family members such as children, parents, spouses, siblings, other family members, or domestic and small business employees.",
      "sources": ["S2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Secondary users can also be IoT devices and software profiles like smart glasses, watches, TVs, and AI profiles under the Full Delegation framework.",
      "sources": ["S7"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A primary user can delegate to up to 5 secondary users, and a secondary user can accept delegation from only one primary user.",
      "sources": ["S3"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Primary users must have visibility of transactions performed by secondary users on their UPI App and bank account statement.",
      "sources": ["S4"]
    }
  ],
  "layout": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "claim_indices": [1, 2, 3]
    },
    {
      "type": "bullets",
      "claim_indices": [4, 5, 6, 7]
    }
  ]
}

